# ==============================================================================
# APPLICATION LOGOS
# ==============================================================================
# Brand marks for the Software grid, vendored as SVG path data so the built
# script stays a single self-contained file: no image files to ship, no network
# access to draw a tile, and the marks scale crisply at any tile size.
#
# Each entry is looked up by the module Key from src/registry.ps1, and is one
# of three shapes (Compile.ps1 enforces this):
#   Color + Data - SVG path data drawn as a WPF Path with the brand colour as
#           fill. Source: simple-icons (github.com/simpleicons/simpleicons),
#           except PowerShell, Java, and Visual Studio, which come from devicon
#           (github.com/devicons/devicon) because simple-icons dropped them.
#           Marks render from any coordinate grid: the tile stretches uniformly.
#   Png     - base64 PNG bytes from the publisher's own repository (app icon,
#           org avatar, or documented logo asset), drawn as a WPF Image with
#           aspect preserved. Used where no single-path vector mark exists.
#   Shapes  - an array of fill/stroke sub-paths for a mark that is not one flat
#           shape (currently only ZapFast, whose badge flattens the official
#           logo.svg gradients). Same Path pipeline, one element per shape.
#   Mono  - initials for a component with no trustworthy mark upstream. Drawn
#           on a neutral tile in theme colours, so nothing here invents a
#           brand colour for someone else's product. Last resort only.
#
# The two hand-authored Data marks (Bibata cursor arrow, game-runtimes gamepad)
# use a neutral grey for the same reason: they are semantic glyphs, not brands.
#
# A module with no entry at all still renders: the grid falls back to the
# label's initials. So adding software to src/registry.ps1 never needs a
# matching row here to keep the UI intact.
#
# Regenerate with the vendoring helper rather than editing by hand.

